{
  "id": "occasional-cause",
  "term": "occasional cause",
  "definition": "An occasional cause is, in occasionalism, an event in mind or matter that does not directly produce a change in the other but serves as the occasion for God to bring about the corresponding change. Thus each side is treated as only the cue for the other, not its true efficient cause.",
